sections.OBJECTS:
table  documents
    Text chunk with metadata and a 1536-dimension embedding.
fn     match_documents(query_embedding vector, filter jsonb) -> TABLE(id uuid, content text, metadata jsonb, similarity double precision)
    Return documents matching a metadata filter, ordered by cosine distance to the query embedding.
fn     search_documents(query_embedding vector, match_threshold double precision, match_count integer, metadata_filter jsonb) -> TABLE(id text, content text, metadata jsonb, similarity double precision)
    Return up to match_count documents whose similarity to the query embedding is above match_threshold.

sections.HOW IT FITS:
utils_common/waba_es/onboarding_utils.py stores each embedded-signup callback (phone number id, WABA id,
  business id, auth code, business token). business_ref ties the row to a restaurant. Read back during onboarding;
  see utils_common/waba_es/embedded_signup_guide.md.

sections.OBJECTS:
fn     job_create_dispatch() -> TABLE(action text)
    Create the next batch of offers for every open delivery option, or time the vehicle type out; returns what it did.
fn     get_available_riders(p_order_number text, p_town text, p_vehicle_type text) -> TABLE(rider_id character varying, priority integer)
    Return the riders (rider_id, priority) who may be offered this order for this town and vehicle type.

sections.SECURITY:
Every function is revoked from PUBLIC/anon/authenticated: only the service key can call them.
Concurrency: one conditional UPDATE decides each tap; receipt copies are claimed in SQL (state 'taken', FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED);
  a claim not finished within 30 s is offered again; a newer receipt only deletes OLDER ones (id <).
